Tests never reach the real site-worker; the hero shows its photograph until the video plays

Two changes, one commit each.

Tests and the site-worker. Cloudflare showed site-worker at 937 invocations in a day, with a usage
meter at about half, while nobody uses the worker yet. It was the tests: they planted their fake
worker by replacing the literal `"brokerUrl": ""`, which stopped matching once `site_worker.yml` named
the real worker, so authorize, devices, settings and upload talked to it instead. Every `/challenge`
is a KV write (1,000 a day on the free tier), and each full run made about 80; CI on every push did
the same.

- `site/tests/fixtures.js` is every spec's `test`: Playwright's, plus an automatic guard that blocks
  any request to `site-worker.*.workers.dev` or `cloud.fcpublicmedia.org` and fails the test that
  made it.
- The swap replaces whatever URL is baked in. Authorize, devices, settings and upload default to no
  worker; the tests that want one plant `broker.test` on top.

The hero on a phone. The poster was the video's first frame, the worst one, and a phone that declines
to autoplay (Low Power Mode, data saver) showed it frozen until play.

- No poster: `hero_video_poster` and `wix-was-poster.jpg` are gone.
- The video is invisible until frames are actually moving (`playing`, not `play`), so the photograph
  shows until then, and again on pause. Reduced motion gets no fade.
- The play/pause icon follows the button's own state, so a tap answers at once while it loads.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] authorize, devices, settings, upload: 108 pass, no request reaches the real worker
- [x] the hero, in Chrome as an iPhone 13: autoplay declined shows the photograph; play shows the
      video; pause returns to the photograph; autoplay allowed plays
- [ ] upload's "produces an entry the site template would accept" needs PyYAML, which CI installs and
      the LAN Mac's python3 lacks

Carried, not decided:
- `meet-board.spec.js` still describes the old /meet/ board block and fails against the new page.
- The home page's contrast check and its hero-video request fail as before.
